00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  apex legend celebrates its first  birthday with the start of season 4  assimilation  if you haven't played the game since it  launched you're in for quite the  surprise if you decide to jump in now  with apex legends going into its year -  we figured it was the perfect time to  look back and see just how much the game  has changed on February 4th 2019 respawn  revealed its new titanfall game was not  actually titanfall 3 as many expected  instead we were getting a free to play  battle royale that takes place within  the titanfall universe it was called  apex legends a fun little nod to Titan  Falls BLISK and his apex predators and  then responded something rather odd it  said the game was now out just  immediately ready to download on Xbox  one ps4 and PC no fanfare no year-long  campaign of trailers and conference  appearances just an announcement and  release and that somehow someway worked  apex legend sought 25 million players  within its first week with two million  peak concurrent users like titanfall 2  the shooting and movement mechanics and  map design were solid fans fell in love  with the diverse cast of characters as  well as the welcome improvements respawn  made to the battle royale formula with  the ping system and hero abilities were  there bugs to fix and balancing changes  to implement sure but apex legends  offered enough to keep players coming  back those first few weeks on February  13th respawn released an update that  included limited time Valentine's Day  themed cosmetics our first hint that  apex legends would do in game  celebrations for certain holidays a week  later on February 20th apex legends got  its first new weapon the havoc assault  rifle those first week suggested respawn  would regularly update the game with new  content and fans began eagerly waiting  for something more did this mean a  battle passives a minute challenges not  yet a month after apex legends released  respawn announced the game had 50  million players and the developer  released a video thinking it's community  the video also jokingly poked fun at the  Mozambique shotgun which was apex  legends worst gun at lot  if anything it seems to suggest respawn  was at least listening to its community  and working on the problems that fans  were bringing up but the novelty of the  game began to wane around this time apex  legend still had no challenges or battle  past a speaker there wasn't really  anything to strive for other than just  getting better at the game  apex legends would finally get a battle  pass on March 19th with the start of  season 1 wild frontier the first season  added a new character to Achtung the  backstory of the idiotic daredevil  provided a nostalgic tied to titanfall 2  when speedrunners tried to break the  record on the titan pilot gauntlet his  abilities weren't exactly game-changing  but Octane's playfully reckless  personality still makes him one of the  most enjoyable add-ons to apex legends  apex legend still didn't have challenges  though and without challenges it was  very difficult to level up in the battle  Paz granted that first pass didn't have  the best rewards anyway in the following  weeks respawn would go on to implement  gameplay adjustments like a new  fortified passive perk for Gibraltar  encaustic as well as bug fixes but  nothing substantial unless you were on  PC of course respawn used this time to  put a serious dent in the hackers and  cheaters that had been dominating the PC  version of the game months would go by  this long dry spell would see some  players drop the game including me if  I'm being honest eleven weeks after the  start of wild frontier apex legends  finally got new content  June 4th saw the start of wild frontiers  first and only limited time event  legendary hunt the event made it easier  to level up in wild frontiers battle  pass better yet it provided a good  reason to even buy the pass in the first  place battle fest owners could nab some  sweet-looking legendary rewards during  legendary hunt players came back it was  the shot in the arm that apex legends  needed before season 2 started respawn  also began fleshing out apex legends  story on June 8th respawn released the  first of its stories from the Outlands a  collection of animated shorts on June  12th the apex legends Twitter account  made its first story focused week  marking the point when the account would  occasionally adopt the persona of a news  anchor that existed within the titanfall  apex Legends universe small map changes  also  and hinting at upcoming story  developments on June 27th respawn  released the cinematic trailer for apex  legend season 2 battle charge which  confirmed a mysterious hacker was taking  an interest in the apex games and the  Flyers and leviathans were now invading  the arena battle charge began on July  2nd implementing the game's first major  map changes it also added a new  character and weapon a pattern all  subsequent seasons would take new  character Watson was a game-changing  addition to apex legends the game's true  first defender Watson could easily lock  down his own and outright negate the  abilities of certain characters she's  still a dominant force on the  competitive side of the game battle  charge was a turning point for apex  legends not only did it finally deliver  on daily and weekly challenges it  introduced a battle pass with worthwhile  rewards rank was also added as a  permanent mode in both in-game events  and cinematic trailers further fleshed  out apex legends lore there was always  something to do during battle charge  whether that was a new lemon-thyme the  vent to play new story details to  discuss or battle past levels to earn  that said battle charge wasn't all  positive during the iron crown  collection event apex legends had a  microtransaction controversy the events  cosmetics were initially solely tied to  loot boxes that did not make people  happy so respawn quickly implemented a  hotfix that made it so you could buy the  events cosmetics individually as well  that seemed to work people stopped  grumbling about the loot boxes since  then respawn has always implemented this  system every event that has cosmetics  and loot boxes allows you to straight up  just by individual cosmetics - if you  don't want to take the chance battle  charge was followed by meltdown which  introduced the long T's crypto as a  playable character another new weapon  and once again implemented challenges  and a battle pass whatever instead of  map changes apex legends got a whole new  map world's edge that fundamentally  altered how teams had to work together  to win the new worlds edge map  emphasized movement more so than the  original Kings Canyon the most surefire  way to find high tier loot was to chase  down the moving train or shoot down one  of the flying cargo BOTS to find a key  to a vault because of the maps larger  size you also had to typically account  for traveling a longer distance when the  ring began to shrink it suddenly became  much more important to have a  on your team who could quickly get your  squad from one spot to another not every  player liked the change but world's edge  and to a greater sense all of season 3  was an example of how respawn was  willing to experiment with apex legends  formula the halloween-themed Fighter  fright event showcased how apex legends  might look with two maps at once the  Christmas themed holiday bash introduced  apex legends first game mode that wasn't  a battle royale and the Roaring Twenties  themed grand soiree arcade saw seven  modes rotated into the game some of  which offered very new ways to play  which brings us to season four  assimilation in the start of year two a  lot sure has changed but what makes apex  legends so fun is still the same that  Chase to be number one  if you're having trouble with your own  journey to becoming a legend GameSpot  has videos on how to play with year ones  11 characters and more guides on the way  for apex legends season 4  [Music]

